* Models of the digital lines and the monitors, written for this project.
* None of these is a model of a manufacturer. Every figure names its
* datasheet and page; a figure that no datasheet gives says "assumption".
* Parts of other sheets that hang on these lines (converter, DAC, gate
* drivers, regulators that are switched off) have a model of their pins
* here under a name of this block; the benches name them through overrides.

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
* Ideal delay: a matched 50 ohm line with a gain of 1.
.subckt DIGITAL_DLY in out params: td=1n
E1 a 0 in 0 2
R1 a b 50
T1 b 0 c 0 Z0=50 TD={td}
R2 c 0 50
E2 out 0 c 0 1
.ends DIGITAL_DLY

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
* Protection diode of a CMOS pin. The datasheets state ratings such as
* "VDD + 0.6 V" and no curve: 0.6 V at 1 mA with 10 ohm in series is an
* assumption (the analog input model of the MCP3208, DS21298E page 18,
* draws its pin diodes with a threshold of 0.6 V).
.model DIGITAL_PIN_D D(IS=8.3e-14 N=1 RS=10)

* A logic input as its absolute maximum ratings describe it: a capacitance
* and a diode to each rail. Used for the pins of parts of other sheets:
* MCP4921 (DS22248A page 2: VSS - 0.3 V to VDD + 0.3 V, 2 mA at an input
* pin; page 7: 10 pF typical), TC4427 (DS20001422G page 2: VDD + 0.3 V to
* GND - 5 V), MUX509 (SBAS758C, digital pins).
*   cin: 10 pF is the MCP4921 figure; other parts give none (assumption).
*   Not modelled: the function behind the pin, leakage.
.subckt DIGITAL_INPUT_PIN pin vdd gnd params: cin=10p
Cin pin gnd {cin}
Dup pin vdd DIGITAL_PIN_D
Ddn gnd pin DIGITAL_PIN_D
.ends DIGITAL_INPUT_PIN

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
* BAT54S, one diode of the pair (D24). onsemi BAT54SLT1/D rev. 18, page 2,
* each diode at 25 C: forward voltage 0.22 V typical and 0.24 V at most at
* 0.1 mA, 0.29 V and 0.32 V at 1 mA, 0.35 V and 0.40 V at 10 mA, 0.41 V and
* 0.50 V at 30 mA, 0.52 V and 0.80 V at 100 mA; reverse current 0.15 uA
* typical and 2 uA at most at 25 V; capacitance 7.6 pF typical at 1 V.
* Page 3: 0.335 V at 0.1 mA and -40 C, 0.125 V at 85 C (figure 2), which
* EG = 0.69 and XTI = 2 reproduce; 13.5 pF at 0 V and 4.5 pF at 5 V
* (figure 4).
*   DIGITAL_BAT54S        typical forward curve
*   DIGITAL_BAT54S_HI     forward voltage at the maximum at 1 mA and 10 mA
*   DIGITAL_BAT54S_LEAKY  reverse current of 2 uA, the maximum; its
*                         forward voltage is too low and means nothing
*   The reverse current of the first two is their saturation current, 20 nA
*   and 25 nA, the order of the typical curve at 1 V (figure 3: 30 nA).
*   Not modelled: the rise of the reverse current with the voltage.
.model DIGITAL_BAT54S       D(IS=2.0e-8 N=1.0 RS=1.2 CJO=13.5p VJ=0.3 M=0.39
+ EG=0.69 XTI=2 BV=30 IBV=10u)
.model DIGITAL_BAT54S_HI    D(IS=2.47e-8 N=1.162 RS=1.2 CJO=13.5p VJ=0.3 M=0.39
+ EG=0.69 XTI=2 BV=30 IBV=10u)
.model DIGITAL_BAT54S_LEAKY D(IS=2.0e-6 N=1.0 RS=1.2 CJO=13.5p VJ=0.3 M=0.39
+ EG=0.69 XTI=2 BV=30 IBV=10u)

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
* 1N5819HW (D1 of the controller sheet). Diodes Incorporated DS30217
* rev. 22-2, page 2 at 25 C: forward voltage at most 0.32 V at 0.1 A and
* 0.45 V at 1 A; reverse current 10 uA typical and 50 uA at most at 4 V,
* 15 uA and 75 uA at 6 V, 1 mA typical at 4 V and 100 C; 50 pF typical at
* 4 V. Page 3, figure 1, typical: 0.15 V at 1 mA, 0.29 V at 0.1 A, 0.40 V
* at 1 A; figure 3: 110 pF at 0 V.
*   The reverse current is the saturation current of 4 uA plus a resistor:
*   rleak = 1 Mohm gives 8 uA at 4 V (typical), rleak = 87 kohm gives 50 uA
*   at 4 V and 73 uA at 6 V (the maxima of the datasheet).
*   Pins: anode, cathode.
.subckt DIGITAL_1N5819HW a k params: rleak=1meg
D1 a k DIGITAL_1N5819_D
Rl a k {rleak}
.ends DIGITAL_1N5819HW
.model DIGITAL_1N5819_D D(IS=4u N=1.05 RS=0.07 CJO=110p VJ=1 M=0.49 EG=0.69
+ XTI=2 BV=40 IBV=1m)

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
* TPD4E1U06, four lines to one clamp (U35, U36, U37). TI SLVSBQ9D.
* Page 8, figure 9: each line has a diode up to an inner rail and a diode
* up from ground; one clamp from the inner rail to ground. Page 5:
* breakdown 6.5 V to 8.5 V at 1 mA, dynamic resistance 1.0 ohm line to
* ground and 0.6 ohm ground to line, 0.8 pF per line at 2.5 V, leakage 1 nA
* typical and 10 nA at most at 2.5 V. Page 6: forward 0.75 V at 1 mA
* (figure 5); pulsed 13 V at 6 A, 18.5 V at 12 A and 24 V at 18 A (figure 1),
* 7 V at 9 A backward (figure 2).
*   vbr: breakdown at 1 mA; the datasheet gives no typical value (its
*   figure 5 shows 8.4 V for one part). 7.5 V is the middle of the limits.
*   Not modelled: leakage (the inner rail has 100 Gohm to ground so that it
*   is a node), the heating that lifts the clamp to 11 V at 1 A and 15 V
*   at 3 A in a surge of 8/20 us (page 5), the destruction of the part.
*   Pins: the four lines, ground. Pin 5 of the package is not connected.
.subckt DIGITAL_TPD4E1U06 io1 io2 io3 io4 gnd params: vbr=7.5
D1u io1 rail DIGITAL_TPD_UP
D1d gnd io1 DIGITAL_TPD_DN
D2u io2 rail DIGITAL_TPD_UP
D2d gnd io2 DIGITAL_TPD_DN
D3u io3 rail DIGITAL_TPD_UP
D3d gnd io3 DIGITAL_TPD_DN
D4u io4 rail DIGITAL_TPD_UP
D4d gnd io4 DIGITAL_TPD_DN
Dz rail zk DIGITAL_TPD_Z
Vz zk gnd {vbr - 1.5}
Rr rail gnd 100g
.ends DIGITAL_TPD4E1U06
.model DIGITAL_TPD_UP D(IS=2.5e-16 N=1 RS=0.45 CJO=0.5p VJ=0.7 M=0.3)
.model DIGITAL_TPD_DN D(IS=2.5e-16 N=1 RS=0.6 CJO=0.5p VJ=0.7 M=0.3)
.model DIGITAL_TPD_Z  D(IS=2.5e-16 N=1 RS=0.45 CJO=30p)

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
* SN74LVC8T245, the direction that the board uses: B port in, A port out
* (U38). TI SCES584D.
*   Input (page 7): low below 0.35 x VCCB and high above 0.65 x VCCB at
*   1.65 V to 1.95 V, 0.7 V and 1.7 V at 2.3 V to 2.7 V, 0.8 V and 2.0 V at
*   3.0 V to 3.6 V, 0.3 x VCCB and 0.7 x VCCB at 4.5 V to 5.5 V. The
*   threshold of the model is kth x VCCB; kth = 0.5 is an assumption inside
*   those limits. Pin capacitance 8.5 pF typical, 10 pF at most (page 9).
*   Ratings (page 6): -0.5 V to 6.5 V at a pin whatever the supplies are,
*   50 mA in the clamp of an input below ground. The pin has a diode to
*   ground and none to its supply. What it does above 6.5 V is not stated:
*   vpos is the level of an assumed clamp of the pin itself and is far
*   away by default.
*   Output (page 9): 2.4 V at least with 24 mA at 3 V, 0.55 V at most, so
*   25 ohm at the most; ro = 20 ohm is an assumption.
*   Delay B to A with 3.3 V on the A side (page 11): 0.8 ns to 7.2 ns with
*   1.8 V on the B side, 0.7 ns to 6.1 ns with 3.3 V, 0.6 ns to 6.0 ns with
*   5 V, into 15 pF. tpd = 3 ns is an assumption inside those limits.
*   Supply of the B side (page 9): 8 uA at the most at rest (iccb); page 11:
*   power-dissipation capacitance 2 pF per input up to 3.3 V and 3 pF at
*   5 V (cpd), drawn as the charge of a capacitor at every rising edge.
*   Isolation (page 15): with a supply below 0.1 V the outputs are open.
*   Not modelled: the direction A to B, the supply current of the A side,
*   leakage (1 uA at 25 C, 2 uA over temperature, page 9), the behaviour
*   between 0.1 V and 1.65 V, which the datasheet does not specify either.
*   Pins in the order of the package.
.subckt DIGITAL_LVC8T245 vcca dir a1 a2 a3 a4 a5 a6 a7 a8 g1 g2 g3
+ b8 b7 b6 b5 b4 b3 b2 b1 oe vccb vccb2
+ params: kth=0.5 tpd=3n ro=20 cio=8.5p cpd=2p iccb=8u vpos=1000
Rg2 g2 g1 1m
Rg3 g3 g1 1m
Rvb vccb2 vccb 1m
Ben1 en1 0 V = 0.5*(1 + tanh((v(vccb,g1) - 0.1)/0.01))
Ben2 en2 0 V = 0.5*(1 + tanh((v(vcca,g1) - 0.1)/0.01))
Ben3 en3 0 V = 0.5*(1 - tanh((v(oe,g1) - 0.5*v(vcca,g1))/0.05))
Ben4 en4 0 V = 0.5*(1 - tanh((v(dir,g1) - 0.5*v(vcca,g1))/0.05))
Ben en 0 V = v(en1)*v(en2)*v(en3)*v(en4)
Bq vccb g1 I = {iccb}*tanh(v(vccb,g1)/0.2)
Cdir dir g1 4p
Coe oe g1 4p
Rdir dir g1 1e12
Roe oe g1 1e12
X1 b1 a1 vcca vccb g1 en DIGITAL_LVC8T245_CH kth={kth} tpd={tpd} ro={ro} cio={cio} cpd={cpd} vpos={vpos}
X2 b2 a2 vcca vccb g1 en DIGITAL_LVC8T245_CH kth={kth} tpd={tpd} ro={ro} cio={cio} cpd={cpd} vpos={vpos}
X3 b3 a3 vcca vccb g1 en DIGITAL_LVC8T245_CH kth={kth} tpd={tpd} ro={ro} cio={cio} cpd={cpd} vpos={vpos}
X4 b4 a4 vcca vccb g1 en DIGITAL_LVC8T245_CH kth={kth} tpd={tpd} ro={ro} cio={cio} cpd={cpd} vpos={vpos}
X5 b5 a5 vcca vccb g1 en DIGITAL_LVC8T245_CH kth={kth} tpd={tpd} ro={ro} cio={cio} cpd={cpd} vpos={vpos}
X6 b6 a6 vcca vccb g1 en DIGITAL_LVC8T245_CH kth={kth} tpd={tpd} ro={ro} cio={cio} cpd={cpd} vpos={vpos}
X7 b7 a7 vcca vccb g1 en DIGITAL_LVC8T245_CH kth={kth} tpd={tpd} ro={ro} cio={cio} cpd={cpd} vpos={vpos}
X8 b8 a8 vcca vccb g1 en DIGITAL_LVC8T245_CH kth={kth} tpd={tpd} ro={ro} cio={cio} cpd={cpd} vpos={vpos}
.ends DIGITAL_LVC8T245

* One channel of the translator: B pin, A pin, the two supplies, ground,
* and the enable of the package (0 V or 1 V).
.subckt DIGITAL_LVC8T245_CH b a vcca vccb gnd en
+ params: kth=0.5 tpd=3n ro=20 cio=8.5p cpd=2p vpos=1000
.param go={1/ro}
.param gpd=5e-4
Cb b gnd {cio}
Db gnd b DIGITAL_PIN_D
Dp b pk DIGITAL_PIN_D
Vp pk gnd {vpos}
Bs s 0 V = 0.5*(1 + tanh((v(b,gnd) - {kth}*v(vccb,gnd))/0.02))
Rs s sf 100
Cs sf 0 1p
Xd sf sd DIGITAL_DLY td={tpd}
Bq sq 0 V = min(max(v(sd), 0), 1)
* the charge that an edge of the input costs the supply of the B side
Bpu vccb p I = v(vccb,p)*{gpd}*v(sf)
Bpd p gnd I = v(p,gnd)*{gpd}*(1 - v(sf))
Cp p gnd {cpd}
* output stage on the supply of the A side
Boh vcca a I = v(vcca,a)*{go}*v(sq)*v(en)
Bol a gnd I = v(a,gnd)*{go}*(1 - v(sq))*v(en)
Ca a gnd {cio}
Ra a gnd 1e12
.ends DIGITAL_LVC8T245_CH

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
* SN74LV165A, parallel-load shift register (U33, U34). TI SCLS402R.
*   Function (page 11): a low level at the load pin copies the eight
*   inputs, whatever the clock does; with the load pin high a rising edge
*   of the clock shifts toward the input D7, whose stage drives the
*   output. The clock is the OR of the clock pin and the inhibit pin.
*   Delay at 3.3 V into 15 pF (page 7): clock to output 8.6 ns typical at
*   25 C, 1 ns to 18 ns over temperature; load pin to output 9.1 ns typical,
*   18.5 ns at most; input D7 to output 8.9 ns typical, 16.5 ns at most.
*   tclk and tld are the delays to the output stage; the edge of the
*   output adds about 1 ns into 15 pF.
*   Output (page 6): 2.48 V at least with 6 mA at 3 V and 0.44 V at most,
*   so 87 ohm and 73 ohm at the most; ro = 50 ohm is an assumption.
*   Inputs (pages 5 and 6): high above 0.7 x VCC, low below 0.3 x VCC,
*   1.7 pF, 5.5 V whatever the supply is: a diode to ground and none to
*   the supply. The threshold of the model is vth, 1.65 V, half of 3.3 V
*   (assumption inside the limits); it does not follow the supply pin.
*   The time limits that the model does not check and the benches measure
*   (page 6, 3.3 V, -40 C to 85 C): load pulse 9 ns, clock pulse 7 ns, load
*   high 6 ns before the clock, data 8.5 ns before the end of the load.
*   Not modelled: supply current, leakage, the open output without supply.
*   Needs the XSPICE code models of ngspice (digital.cm).
*   Pins in the order of the package.
.subckt DIGITAL_LV165A pl cp d4 d5 d6 d7 qn7 gnd q7 ds d0 d1 d2 d3 ce vcc
+ params: vth=1.65 tclk=7.6n tld=8.0n ro=50 ci=1.7p
.model LVADC adc_bridge(in_low={vth} in_high={vth} rise_delay=10p fall_delay=10p)
.model LVDAC dac_bridge(out_low=0 out_high=1 out_undef=0.5 t_rise=0.4n t_fall=0.4n)
.model LVFF d_dff(clk_delay={tclk} set_delay={tld} reset_delay={tld} ic=0
+ rise_delay=1p fall_delay=1p)
.model LVINV d_inverter(rise_delay=1p fall_delay=1p)
.model LVAND d_and(rise_delay=1p fall_delay=1p)
.model LVOR d_or(rise_delay=1p fall_delay=1p)
Aadc [%vd(pl,gnd) %vd(cp,gnd) %vd(ce,gnd) %vd(ds,gnd) %vd(d0,gnd) %vd(d1,gnd)
+ %vd(d2,gnd) %vd(d3,gnd) %vd(d4,gnd) %vd(d5,gnd) %vd(d6,gnd) %vd(d7,gnd)]
+ [xpl xcp xce xds x0 x1 x2 x3 x4 x5 x6 x7] LVADC
Ald xpl ld LVINV
Ack [xcp xce] ck LVOR
Ai0 x0 n0 LVINV
Ai1 x1 n1 LVINV
Ai2 x2 n2 LVINV
Ai3 x3 n3 LVINV
Ai4 x4 n4 LVINV
Ai5 x5 n5 LVINV
Ai6 x6 n6 LVINV
Ai7 x7 n7 LVINV
As0 [ld x0] s0 LVAND
As1 [ld x1] s1 LVAND
As2 [ld x2] s2 LVAND
As3 [ld x3] s3 LVAND
As4 [ld x4] s4 LVAND
As5 [ld x5] s5 LVAND
As6 [ld x6] s6 LVAND
As7 [ld x7] s7 LVAND
Ar0 [ld n0] r0 LVAND
Ar1 [ld n1] r1 LVAND
Ar2 [ld n2] r2 LVAND
Ar3 [ld n3] r3 LVAND
Ar4 [ld n4] r4 LVAND
Ar5 [ld n5] r5 LVAND
Ar6 [ld n6] r6 LVAND
Ar7 [ld n7] r7 LVAND
Af0 xds ck s0 r0 q0 qb0 LVFF
Af1 q0 ck s1 r1 q1 qb1 LVFF
Af2 q1 ck s2 r2 q2 qb2 LVFF
Af3 q2 ck s3 r3 q3 qb3 LVFF
Af4 q3 ck s4 r4 q4 qb4 LVFF
Af5 q4 ck s5 r5 q5 qb5 LVFF
Af6 q5 ck s6 r6 q6 qb6 LVFF
Af7 q6 ck s7 r7 q7d qb7d LVFF
Adac [q7d qb7d] [y yn] LVDAC
Bo o gnd V = v(vcc,gnd)*min(max(v(y), 0), 1)
Ro o q7 {ro}
Bon on gnd V = v(vcc,gnd)*min(max(v(yn), 0), 1)
Ron on qn7 {ro}
Cpl pl gnd {ci}
Ccp cp gnd {ci}
Cce ce gnd {ci}
Cds ds gnd {ci}
C0 d0 gnd {ci}
C1 d1 gnd {ci}
C2 d2 gnd {ci}
C3 d3 gnd {ci}
C4 d4 gnd {ci}
C5 d5 gnd {ci}
C6 d6 gnd {ci}
C7 d7 gnd {ci}
Dpl gnd pl DIGITAL_PIN_D
Dcp gnd cp DIGITAL_PIN_D
Ripl pl gnd 1e12
Ricp cp gnd 1e12
Rice ce gnd 1e12
Rids ds gnd 1e12
Rid0 d0 gnd 1e12
Rid1 d1 gnd 1e12
Rid2 d2 gnd 1e12
Rid3 d3 gnd 1e12
Rid4 d4 gnd 1e12
Rid5 d5 gnd 1e12
Rid6 d6 gnd 1e12
Rid7 d7 gnd 1e12
Rvc vcc gnd 1e9
Rq7 q7 gnd 1e12
Rqn7 qn7 gnd 1e12
.ends DIGITAL_LV165A

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
* ADS8860, the digital pins in the three-wire mode with DIN high (U30).
* TI SBAS569B.
*   Function (page 22): the rising edge of CONVST starts a conversion and
*   opens DOUT. The falling edge of CONVST puts the first bit on DOUT;
*   every falling edge of SCLK puts the next one; after the 16th falling
*   edge, or when CONVST rises, DOUT is open again.
*   Timing at 3 V (page 8): next bit valid at most 13.4 ns after the
*   falling edge of SCLK (tdo), the bit before it valid for 3 ns at least;
*   first bit at most 12.3 ns after CONVST fell (ten); DOUT open at most
*   13.2 ns after CONVST rose; the model opens it at once. The datasheet
*   gives no typical value.
*   tdo and ten are the delays to the output stage: into the 20 pF of the
*   datasheet the output reaches its level 2 ns later, so the defaults,
*   11.2 ns and 10.2 ns, put the model at the largest delays. tdo = 2.8 ns
*   gives the earliest change, 3 ns after the edge.
*   Conversion 500 ns to 710 ns, quiet time 20 ns: not checked here.
*   Levels (page 7): inputs high above 0.7 x DVDD and low below 0.3 x DVDD;
*   output 0.8 x DVDD and 0.2 x DVDD at 500 uA into 20 pF, which bounds its
*   resistance at 1.2 kohm and says nothing more. Ratings (page 5): pins
*   from -0.3 V to DVDD + 0.3 V, no current figure.
*   Assumptions: ro = 40 ohm, cin = cout = 5 pF, threshold vth 1.65 V, a
*   diode from every pin to DVDD and from ground to every pin.
*   code: the word that is shifted out, 0 to 65535.
*   Not modelled: the converter itself, the supply currents.
*   Needs the XSPICE code models of ngspice (digital.cm).
*   Pins: CONVST, DOUT, SCLK, DIN, DVDD, ground.
.subckt DIGITAL_ADS8860_IO convst dout sclk din dvdd gnd
+ params: code=42435 tdo=11.2n ten=10.2n ro=40 cin=5p cout=5p vth=1.65
.param go={1/ro}
.model ADADC adc_bridge(in_low={vth} in_high={vth} rise_delay=10p fall_delay=10p)
.model ADDAC dac_bridge(out_low=0 out_high=1 out_undef=0.5 t_rise=0.2n t_fall=0.2n)
.model ADINV d_inverter(rise_delay=1p fall_delay=1p)
.model ADAND d_and(rise_delay=1p fall_delay=1p)
.model ADEN d_buffer(rise_delay={ten} fall_delay=1p)
.model ADTFF d_tff(clk_delay={tdo} set_delay=1n reset_delay=1n ic=0
+ rise_delay=1p fall_delay=1p)
.model ADLOW d_pulldown(load=1p)
Aadc [%vd(convst,gnd) %vd(sclk,gnd)] [xcnv xsck] ADADC
Alow zero ADLOW
Ainc xcnv ncnv ADINV
Aink xsck nsck ADINV
* counter of the falling edges of SCLK, held at zero while CONVST is high
At0 nq4 nsck zero xcnv q0 nq0 ADTFF
Aa1 [q0 nq4] t1 ADAND
At1 t1 nsck zero xcnv q1 nq1 ADTFF
Aa2 [q0 q1] t2 ADAND
At2 t2 nsck zero xcnv q2 nq2 ADTFF
Aa3 [q0 q1 q2] t3 ADAND
At3 t3 nsck zero xcnv q3 nq3 ADTFF
Aa4 [q0 q1 q2 q3] t4 ADAND
At4 t4 nsck zero xcnv q4 nq4 ADTFF
* DOUT drives while CONVST is low and fewer than 16 edges have passed
Aen1 ncnv enr ADEN
Aen2 [enr nq4 ncnv] en ADAND
Adac [q0 q1 q2 q3 en] [y0 y1 y2 y3 ye] ADDAC
Bn n 0 V = floor(v(y0) + 2*v(y1) + 4*v(y2) + 8*v(y3) + 0.5)
Bb bit 0 V = floor({code}/pwr(2, 15 - v(n)) + 1e-6) - 2*floor({code}/pwr(2, 16 - v(n)) + 1e-6)
Rb bit bf 100
Cb bf 0 2p
Bs sq 0 V = min(max(v(bf), 0), 1)
Be eq 0 V = min(max(v(ye), 0), 1)
Boh dvdd dout I = v(dvdd,dout)*{go}*v(sq)*v(eq)
Bol dout gnd I = v(dout,gnd)*{go}*(1 - v(sq))*v(eq)
Cout dout gnd {cout}
Rout dout gnd 1e12
Ccnv convst gnd {cin}
Csck sclk gnd {cin}
Cdin din gnd {cin}
Dcu convst dvdd DIGITAL_PIN_D
Dcd gnd convst DIGITAL_PIN_D
Dsu sclk dvdd DIGITAL_PIN_D
Dsd gnd sclk DIGITAL_PIN_D
Diu din dvdd DIGITAL_PIN_D
Did gnd din DIGITAL_PIN_D
Dou dout dvdd DIGITAL_PIN_D
Dod gnd dout DIGITAL_PIN_D
.ends DIGITAL_ADS8860_IO

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
* MCP3208, the inputs and the sampling of the monitor converter (U40).
* Microchip DS21298E.
*   Analog input (page 18, figure 4-1): 7 pF at the pin, a diode with a
*   threshold of 0.6 V to each rail, a sampling switch of 1 kohm and a
*   sampling capacitor of 20 pF. Page 3: leakage 1 nA typical and 1 uA at
*   the most; it is not in the model and a bench adds it as a source.
*   Sampling (page 19): after the start bit, the first clock with the
*   select low and DIN high, four more rising edges take the mode bit and
*   the channel bits D2, D1 and D0. The input is sampled from the fourth
*   of them to the falling edge of the fifth clock after the start bit,
*   1.5 clock cycles.
*   The sampling capacitor keeps its charge between two samples and meets
*   the next channel with the voltage of the one before: an assumption
*   about the capacitor array, which the datasheet does not describe. With
*   reset = 1 the capacitor is set to vres while the select is high, for
*   the worst case of a capacitor that starts far from the input.
*   Digital pins (page 3): high above 0.7 x VDD, low below 0.3 x VDD, 10 pF
*   at the most, leakage 10 uA at the most; page 2: -0.6 V to VDD + 0.6 V.
*   The threshold of the model is vth, 1.65 V (assumption, half of 3.3 V).
*   Not modelled: the conversion and the data output (DOUT is open), the
*   mode bit (single-ended is assumed), offset, gain and linearity errors
*   (3 LSB, 5 LSB and 1 LSB at the most, page 2), the reference current.
*   The voltage held on the node "samp" inside is what a conversion works on.
*   Needs the XSPICE code models of ngspice (digital.cm).
*   Pins in the order of the package.
.subckt DIGITAL_MCP3208 ch0 ch1 ch2 ch3 ch4 ch5 ch6 ch7 dgnd cs din dout clk agnd vref vdd
+ params: rss=1k csamp=20p cpin=7p cdig=10p vth=1.65 reset=0 vres=0
.param gss={1/rss}
.model MCADC adc_bridge(in_low={vth} in_high={vth} rise_delay=10p fall_delay=10p)
.model MCDAC dac_bridge(out_low=0 out_high=1 out_undef=0.5 t_rise=5n t_fall=5n)
.model MCFF d_dff(clk_delay=2n set_delay=2n reset_delay=2n ic=0 rise_delay=1p fall_delay=1p)
.model MCINV d_inverter(rise_delay=1p fall_delay=1p)
.model MCAND d_and(rise_delay=1p fall_delay=1p)
.model MCOR d_or(rise_delay=1p fall_delay=1p)
.model MCLOW d_pulldown(load=1p)
Aadc [%vd(cs,dgnd) %vd(clk,dgnd) %vd(din,dgnd)] [xcs xck xdi] MCADC
Alow zero MCLOW
Ainv xck nck MCINV
* the start bit, then one stage per clock
Aor0 [st xdi] std MCOR
Af0 std xck zero xcs st nst MCFF
Af1 st xck zero xcs s1 ns1 MCFF
Af2 s1 xck zero xcs s2 ns2 MCFF
Af3 s2 xck zero xcs s3 ns3 MCFF
Af4 s3 xck zero xcs s4 ns4 MCFF
Af5 s4 xck zero xcs s5 ns5 MCFF
Af6 s5 nck zero xcs e ne MCFF
Asm [s4 ne] smp MCAND
* the channel bits, shifted in until the sampling starts
Ah0 [s4 b0] h0 MCAND
Ag0 [ns4 xdi] g0 MCAND
Ao0 [h0 g0] b0d MCOR
Ab0 b0d xck zero xcs b0 nb0 MCFF
Ah1 [s4 b1] h1 MCAND
Ag1 [ns4 b0] g1 MCAND
Ao1 [h1 g1] b1d MCOR
Ab1 b1d xck zero xcs b1 nb1 MCFF
Ah2 [s4 b2] h2 MCAND
Ag2 [ns4 b1] g2 MCAND
Ao2 [h2 g2] b2d MCOR
Ab2 b2d xck zero xcs b2 nb2 MCFF
Ae0 [smp nb2 nb1 nb0] e0 MCAND
Ae1 [smp nb2 nb1 b0] e1 MCAND
Ae2 [smp nb2 b1 nb0] e2 MCAND
Ae3 [smp nb2 b1 b0] e3 MCAND
Ae4 [smp b2 nb1 nb0] e4 MCAND
Ae5 [smp b2 nb1 b0] e5 MCAND
Ae6 [smp b2 b1 nb0] e6 MCAND
Ae7 [smp b2 b1 b0] e7 MCAND
Adac [e0 e1 e2 e3 e4 e5 e6 e7 xcs] [y0 y1 y2 y3 y4 y5 y6 y7 yc] MCDAC
Bs0 ch0 samp I = v(ch0,samp)*{gss}*min(max(v(y0), 0), 1)
Bs1 ch1 samp I = v(ch1,samp)*{gss}*min(max(v(y1), 0), 1)
Bs2 ch2 samp I = v(ch2,samp)*{gss}*min(max(v(y2), 0), 1)
Bs3 ch3 samp I = v(ch3,samp)*{gss}*min(max(v(y3), 0), 1)
Bs4 ch4 samp I = v(ch4,samp)*{gss}*min(max(v(y4), 0), 1)
Bs5 ch5 samp I = v(ch5,samp)*{gss}*min(max(v(y5), 0), 1)
Bs6 ch6 samp I = v(ch6,samp)*{gss}*min(max(v(y6), 0), 1)
Bs7 ch7 samp I = v(ch7,samp)*{gss}*min(max(v(y7), 0), 1)
Csamp samp agnd {csamp}
Rsamp samp agnd 1e13
Brs samp agnd I = (v(samp,agnd) - {vres})*1e-3*{reset}*min(max(v(yc), 0), 1)
Cp0 ch0 agnd {cpin}
Cp1 ch1 agnd {cpin}
Cp2 ch2 agnd {cpin}
Cp3 ch3 agnd {cpin}
Cp4 ch4 agnd {cpin}
Cp5 ch5 agnd {cpin}
Cp6 ch6 agnd {cpin}
Cp7 ch7 agnd {cpin}
Du0 ch0 vdd DIGITAL_PIN_D
Dd0 agnd ch0 DIGITAL_PIN_D
Du1 ch1 vdd DIGITAL_PIN_D
Dd1 agnd ch1 DIGITAL_PIN_D
Du2 ch2 vdd DIGITAL_PIN_D
Dd2 agnd ch2 DIGITAL_PIN_D
Du3 ch3 vdd DIGITAL_PIN_D
Dd3 agnd ch3 DIGITAL_PIN_D
Du4 ch4 vdd DIGITAL_PIN_D
Dd4 agnd ch4 DIGITAL_PIN_D
Du5 ch5 vdd DIGITAL_PIN_D
Dd5 agnd ch5 DIGITAL_PIN_D
Du6 ch6 vdd DIGITAL_PIN_D
Dd6 agnd ch6 DIGITAL_PIN_D
Du7 ch7 vdd DIGITAL_PIN_D
Dd7 agnd ch7 DIGITAL_PIN_D
Xcs cs vdd dgnd DIGITAL_INPUT_PIN cin={cdig}
Xck clk vdd dgnd DIGITAL_INPUT_PIN cin={cdig}
Xdi din vdd dgnd DIGITAL_INPUT_PIN cin={cdig}
Xdo dout vdd dgnd DIGITAL_INPUT_PIN cin={cdig}
Rref vref agnd 1e9
Rgg dgnd agnd 1m
.ends DIGITAL_MCP3208

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
* MCP9700A temperature sensor (U39). Microchip DS20001942L, pages 3 and 4:
* 500 mV at 0 C, 10.0 mV per kelvin, accuracy +/-1 C typical and +/-2 C at
* the most from 0 C to 70 C, output impedance 20 ohm at 500 Hz, supply
* 2.3 V to 5.5 V, 6 uA typical.
*   The temperature is that of the simulation plus dt; terr is the error of
*   the part in kelvin.
*   Not modelled: the turn-on time of 0.8 ms, the limit of 100 uA of output
*   current (which the model does not take from the supply pin either), the
*   non-linearity of 0.5 C, noise.
*   Pins: supply, output, ground.
.subckt DIGITAL_MCP9700A vdd vout gnd params: dt=0 terr=0 zout=20 idd=6u
Bt t 0 V = 0.5 + 0.010*(temper + {dt} + {terr})
Bo o gnd V = min(v(t), max(v(vdd,gnd) - 0.1, 0))*0.5*(1 + tanh((v(vdd,gnd) - 2.0)/0.1))
Ro o vout {zout}
Bq vdd gnd I = {idd}*tanh(v(vdd,gnd)/0.2)
.ends DIGITAL_MCP9700A

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
* A pad of the RP2350 as a bench uses it. RP2350 datasheet, table 1683
* (page 1336) at 3.3 V: output 2.62 V at least and 0.5 V at most at the
* current of the drive setting, so 170 ohm and 125 ohm at the most at
* 4 mA, 57 ohm and 42 ohm at 12 mA; input high above 2.0 V, low below
* 0.8 V; pull-down 36 kohm to 113 kohm, pull-up 32 kohm to 86 kohm;
* leakage 1 uA. The datasheet gives no typical output resistance and no
* capacitance.
*   ctl: 1 V for a high level, 0 V for a low one. oe: 1 V drives, 0 V
*   releases the pad.
*   roh, rol: the limits of the 4 mA setting by default.
*   cpad: 5 pF for the pad, its package pin and the socket (assumption).
*   tedge: time constant of the edge inside the pad (assumption).
*   e9 = 1 adds the current of erratum E9 of stepping A2 (page 1358 and
*   figure 157 on page 1359, a typical part with the input enabled): up to
*   115 uA out of a pad that stands between 1.2 V and 2.4 V.
*   Not modelled: the input buffer (the benches read the 0.8 V and 2.0 V
*   limits), the slew setting, the difference between parts.
*   Pins: pad, ctl, oe, the 3.3 V of the module, ground.
.subckt DIGITAL_RP2350_PAD pad ctl oe iovdd gnd
+ params: roh=170 rol=125 cpad=5p rpd=1e12 rpu=1e12 tedge=0.3n e9=0
.param goh={1/roh}
.param gol={1/rol}
.param cedge={tedge/1e3}
Rc ctl cf 1k
Cc cf 0 {cedge}
Ro oe of 1k
Co of 0 {cedge}
Bs s 0 V = min(max(v(cf), 0), 1)
Be e 0 V = min(max(v(of), 0), 1)
Boh iovdd pad I = v(iovdd,pad)*{goh}*v(s)*v(e)
Bol pad gnd I = v(pad,gnd)*{gol}*(1 - v(s))*v(e)
Be9 iovdd pad I = {e9}*pwl(v(pad,gnd), 0,0, 1.2,0, 1.3,115u, 1.4,115u, 1.6,108u,
+ 1.8,98u, 2.0,85u, 2.1,55u, 2.2,22u, 2.3,5u, 2.4,0, 6,0)
Rpd pad gnd {rpd}
Rpu pad iovdd {rpu}
Cp pad gnd {cpad}
Dd gnd pad DIGITAL_PIN_D
.ends DIGITAL_RP2350_PAD

* A standard pad (GP26 to GP28): the same with a diode to the 3.3 V of the
* module (RP2350 datasheet, table 1683: input at most IOVDD + 0.3 V; Pico 2
* datasheet, section 5.2).
.subckt DIGITAL_RP2350_PAD_STD pad ctl oe iovdd gnd
+ params: roh=170 rol=125 cpad=5p rpd=1e12 rpu=1e12 tedge=0.3n e9=0
X1 pad ctl oe iovdd gnd DIGITAL_RP2350_PAD roh={roh} rol={rol} cpad={cpad} rpd={rpd}
+ rpu={rpu} tedge={tedge} e9={e9}
Du pad iovdd DIGITAL_PIN_D
.ends DIGITAL_RP2350_PAD_STD

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
* The supply side of the Raspberry Pi Pico 2 (U1). Pico 2 datasheet,
* figure 7 on page 15: VBUS feeds VSYS through the Schottky diode D1,
* PMEG6010ELR; R10, 5.6 kohm, and R1, 10 kohm, go from VBUS to ground with
* GP24 between them; 47 uF on VSYS; a buck-boost regulator from 1.8 V on.
* Diode (Nexperia PMEG6010ELR of 1 January 2023, page 4, typical at 25 C):
* 475 mV at 0.1 A, 605 mV at 1 A, reverse current 5 nA at 5 V.
*   pload: what the module takes, as a constant power. Tables 1 and 2 of
*   the Pico 2 datasheet (page 13) give 27 mW to 71 mW for its examples;
*   0.1 W is an assumption for a program that uses both cores.
*   Pins: VBUS, VSYS, ground. The node gp24 inside is the VBUS sense pin.
.subckt DIGITAL_PICO2_SUPPLY vbus vsys gnd params: pload=0.1
D1 vbus vsys DIGITAL_PMEG6010
R10 vbus gp24 5.6k
R1 gp24 gnd 10k
C1 vsys gnd 47u
Bl vsys gnd I = {pload}/max(v(vsys,gnd), 1.5)*0.5*(1 + tanh((v(vsys,gnd) - 1.8)/0.05))
.ends DIGITAL_PICO2_SUPPLY
.model DIGITAL_PMEG6010 D(IS=3.4n N=1.05 RS=0.075 CJO=120p EG=0.69 XTI=2 BV=60 IBV=1m)

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
* LP5907 switched off (U7 and U8 while the supervisor holds the carrier
* off). TI SNVS798Q, page 5: with the enable pin low the output is
* discharged through 230 ohm (typical). Nothing else of the regulator is
* in this model.
*   Pins: input, output, ground.
.subckt DIGITAL_LP5907_OFF in out gnd params: rad=230
Rad out gnd {rad}
Rin in gnd 1e9
.ends DIGITAL_LP5907_OFF
